# Git LFS for the binaries that live INSIDE this project.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS RATHER THAN A LINE IN THE ROOT .gitattributes
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# The root file already routes client media to LFS, but every one of its
# patterns contains a slash — `assets/**/*.png` and friends — and a pattern
# with a slash is anchored to the directory of the .gitattributes that
# declares it. So `assets/**/*.png` at the repo root matches
# <repo>/assets/... and nothing under tv-menu/. Verified with:
#
#     git check-attr filter -- tv-menu/motion/hyperframes/assets/backgrounds/LS_Menu_Background_v01.png
#     -> filter: unspecified
#
# Rules here are anchored to THIS directory, which is what we want, and the
# root file is left alone — it currently carries uncommitted changes from
# another session (LFS rules for brand/), and editing it would drag that
# unfinished work into this project's commits.
#
# WHAT GOES THROUGH LFS
# ---------------------
# Only real binaries. The compositions, the CSS, the scripts and the JSON are
# text whose diffs are the point of having them in git at all.

# The 6 client-selected images that exist nowhere else in the workspace.
# The other 40 are reached through symlinks to files the repo already owns —
# see data/image-paths.json — so they are NOT stored again here.
assets/selected/*.png  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# The client-approved menu artwork the whole video is painted on.
assets/backgrounds/*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# The self-hosted brand typeface. Small, but binary, and regenerated by
# scripts/build-brand-css.py rather than hand-edited.
assets/fonts/*.woff2   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
